00:16:49.200 --> 00:16:51.303
I just wanna say, I get that,

00:16:53.186 --> 00:16:55.560
and I still love your stuff.

00:16:55.560 --> 00:16:56.790
I still respect everything you've done."

00:16:56.790 --> 00:16:58.830
And that was like just a genuine,

00:16:58.830 --> 00:17:02.070
okay I met like a few people
at the bar, at the hotel,

00:17:02.070 --> 00:17:04.410
who I just had just had a
genuine conversation with

00:17:04.410 --> 00:17:07.807
from like that starting
point, where, you know,

00:17:07.807 --> 00:17:08.940
"We acknowledge this,

00:17:08.940 --> 00:17:10.560
but I still wanna get to know this person

00:17:10.560 --> 00:17:13.050
because we're in a environment
where I can get to have

00:17:13.050 --> 00:17:15.180
a more chilled conversation about it."

00:17:15.180 --> 00:17:19.830
But then, you do just get
these one or two maybe fans

00:17:19.830 --> 00:17:23.253
who just don't watch Trash
Taste as often as other people.

00:17:24.120 --> 00:17:26.700
'Cause especially like
reading the subreddit

00:17:26.700 --> 00:17:28.710
and reading how much people
have called this out,

00:17:28.710 --> 00:17:29.737
I'm just like,

00:17:29.737 --> 00:17:30.840
"That's fuckin' great."
(clapping hands)

00:17:30.840 --> 00:17:32.580
Unfortunately, not everyone of our viewers

00:17:32.580 --> 00:17:34.410
is on the subreddit, for example.

00:17:34.410 --> 00:17:37.020
Not every viewer watches every episode.

00:17:37.020 --> 00:17:38.490
So you will get that casual viewer

00:17:38.490 --> 00:17:41.220
who just doesn't know more,

00:17:41.220 --> 00:17:42.450
like doesn't know about the boundaries

00:17:42.450 --> 00:17:44.305
as much as like other viewers, I think.

00:17:44.305 --> 00:17:45.138
- I dunno.

00:17:45.138 --> 00:17:46.386
I mean, to me it was like,

00:17:46.386 --> 00:17:48.180
this is just all a learning experience.

00:17:48.180 --> 00:17:49.560
Like this is no way made me

00:17:49.560 --> 00:17:50.910
not wanna go to cons or anything.

00:17:50.910 --> 00:17:53.145
- [Garnt and Joey] No, no, no.

00:17:53.145 --> 00:17:55.080
- Like we've said this a
million times, but yeah,

00:17:55.080 --> 00:17:57.150
everyone was super fuckin' nice.

00:17:57.150 --> 00:17:58.500
The signings were great.

00:17:58.500 --> 00:17:59.970
Everyone was really respectful,

00:17:59.970 --> 00:18:01.470
except you got shot by a Nerf
gun by someone. (laughing)

00:18:01.470 --> 00:18:02.303
- Yeah.

00:18:02.303 --> 00:18:05.111
- Yeah, that wasn't cool.
I wasn't there to see, but-

00:18:05.111 --> 00:18:06.300
- So, it was 'cause it's like open, right?

00:18:06.300 --> 00:18:07.133
- Yeah, it was open.

00:18:07.133 --> 00:18:08.730
- So, we had like a table,
and there was three of us.

00:18:08.730 --> 00:18:10.140
I was in the middle, Joey was on the end,

00:18:10.140 --> 00:18:12.060
and then there's Garnt on this end.

00:18:12.060 --> 00:18:13.710
And this end is completely open,

00:18:13.710 --> 00:18:16.560
so anyone could have walked up
and thrown anything at Garnt,

00:18:16.560 --> 00:18:17.700
which is just an oversight.

00:18:17.700 --> 00:18:21.637
They should have had someone
there who is stopping this.

00:18:21.637 --> 00:18:23.760
- I think it was like...

00:18:23.760 --> 00:18:24.593
It's a learning experience.

00:18:24.593 --> 00:18:27.480
It's not just for us, but
for the convention itself,

00:18:27.480 --> 00:18:28.410
for the convention as well.

00:18:28.410 --> 00:18:32.190
So like, I remember the
conversation where we talked about,

00:18:32.190 --> 00:18:33.810
we don't know if we need security

00:18:33.810 --> 00:18:35.670
for future conventions yet.

00:18:35.670 --> 00:18:37.438
This taught us that we definitely do need-

00:18:37.438 --> 00:18:38.640
- [Joey] Yeah, we
definitely do. (laughing)

00:18:38.640 --> 00:18:40.140
We definitely do need security.

00:18:40.140 --> 00:18:43.530
Like that was like a very
much a big eye opener for us.

00:18:43.530 --> 00:18:46.260
- I mean, obviously we
had the incident happened

00:18:46.260 --> 00:18:49.380
where someone came on the
stage, who apparently...

00:18:49.380 --> 00:18:51.430
Okay, so this is the whole fuckin' thing.

00:18:53.280 --> 00:18:54.750
You said it was a learning
experience with the convention.

00:18:54.750 --> 00:18:55.920
I feel like, I don't know,

00:18:55.920 --> 00:18:58.530
they should know that
it would've been better.

00:18:58.530 --> 00:19:00.030
And to be fair, they stepped it up,

00:19:00.030 --> 00:19:02.580
but I feel like it should
have been there anyway.

00:19:02.580 --> 00:19:05.850
We practically had no security really

00:19:05.850 --> 00:19:07.140
for like the first two days.

00:19:07.140 --> 00:19:10.230
- Yeah, I think they definitely
should have had security

00:19:10.230 --> 00:19:11.160
for the panel.

00:19:11.160 --> 00:19:14.970
But I talked to some people
afterwards, who working there,

00:19:14.970 --> 00:19:19.620
and they said, "This has
never happened before.

00:19:19.620 --> 00:19:21.750
This has never even
become close to happening.

00:19:21.750 --> 00:19:24.690
There was never like a precedence

00:19:24.690 --> 00:19:27.000
of this like ever happening at MCM."

00:19:27.000 --> 00:19:29.580
So it was also, it wasn't oversight,

00:19:29.580 --> 00:19:32.707
but also, like a lot of
people just didn't expect it

00:19:32.707 --> 00:19:35.430
'cause it just never happened before.

00:19:35.430 --> 00:19:38.070
- I mean, yeah, I agree, and
I don't wanna go too hard,

00:19:38.070 --> 00:19:40.980
'cause obviously, like we
wanna go to cons again,

00:19:40.980 --> 00:19:43.860
but like it blows my mind

00:19:43.860 --> 00:19:45.960
that you would have a main stage event

00:19:45.960 --> 00:19:48.843
and not have like at least
one scary dude in the front,

00:19:49.967 --> 00:19:52.050
'cause like it was anyone
could have come up,

00:19:52.050 --> 00:19:53.790
everyone could have come up. (chuckles)

00:19:53.790 --> 00:19:58.140
- And it's still like MCM
haven't had insanely large guests

00:19:58.140 --> 00:19:58.973
in the past.

00:19:58.973 --> 00:20:00.690
So I'm thinking like, "What do they do-"

00:20:00.690 --> 00:20:01.830
- Well, they had like Tom Hiddleston.

00:20:01.830 --> 00:20:04.200
- Yeah, and it's like
there's no way Tom Hiddleston

00:20:04.200 --> 00:20:05.220
could do a panel on stage,

00:20:05.220 --> 00:20:07.560
and there wouldn't be a single
fuckin' bodyguard anywhere.

00:20:07.560 --> 00:20:10.067
- I dunno, maybe it's just
like a thing of they're like,

00:20:10.067 --> 00:20:11.370
"All right, well we have
some guests this year.

00:20:11.370 --> 00:20:12.840
None of them are super high profile.

00:20:12.840 --> 00:20:15.060
I guess we can scale it
back, save some money."

00:20:15.060 --> 00:20:16.747
But obviously, you know.

00:20:16.747 --> 00:20:20.310
And also, a lot of these cons,
they know YouTubers are big.

00:20:20.310 --> 00:20:22.020
They know it, but they don't like,

00:20:22.020 --> 00:20:23.220
they don't know it, right? (chuckles)

00:20:23.220 --> 00:20:24.900
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.
- Yeah.

00:20:24.900 --> 00:20:27.180
- They understand, "Oh,
yes, 3 million subs,"

00:20:27.180 --> 00:20:28.013
but they're like,

00:20:28.013 --> 00:20:29.370
"Yeah, but we have the guy who voices

00:20:29.370 --> 00:20:31.257
in 'The Fairly Oddparents,' here.

00:20:31.257 --> 00:20:33.330
And I know what that is.

00:20:33.330 --> 00:20:35.610
And I don't know who this Trash guy is.

00:20:35.610 --> 00:20:36.443
Who's these rubbish rubbish boys?"

00:20:36.443 --> 00:20:37.320
- The rubbish lads.

00:20:37.320 --> 00:20:38.492
- Yeah, who's these rubbish lads?

00:20:38.492 --> 00:20:39.840
(Garnt laughing)
What are they?

00:20:39.840 --> 00:20:41.310
So there's this complete...

00:20:41.310 --> 00:20:42.480
Like a lot of cons do have

00:20:42.480 --> 00:20:44.340
this kind of disconnect between like...

00:20:44.340 --> 00:20:47.310
Because a lot of the
cons are ran by people

00:20:47.310 --> 00:20:50.550
who understand older media
and traditional media,

00:20:50.550 --> 00:20:53.640
they don't really understand
YouTubers that well.

00:20:53.640 --> 00:20:55.710
They should buy now, but they don't.

00:20:55.710 --> 00:20:57.150
And so I feel like
there's a lot of oversight

00:20:57.150 --> 00:20:58.380
that happened there.

00:20:58.380 --> 00:21:00.630
And then getting to
this guy in particular,

00:21:00.630 --> 00:21:03.120
who came on the stage,
which was a weird thing,

00:21:03.120 --> 00:21:06.000
'cause this guy didn't do
anything for the first 20 minutes.

00:21:06.000 --> 00:21:06.833
- Yeah.

00:21:06.833 --> 00:21:09.180
- And then started shouting.

00:21:09.180 --> 00:21:10.860
- Everyone thought he
was like just a heckler.

00:21:10.860 --> 00:21:11.693
- Yeah, yeah.

00:21:11.693 --> 00:21:12.930
- I thought he was a heckler,

00:21:12.930 --> 00:21:14.257
'cause I was just like,

00:21:14.257 --> 00:21:16.123
"We've all dealt with
hecklers in the past as well."

00:21:16.123 --> 00:21:16.956
- [Joey] Yeah, of course.

00:21:16.956 --> 00:21:20.100
- So, someone asked a question,

00:21:20.100 --> 00:21:23.010
and then I just like heard
someone shouting something

00:21:23.010 --> 00:21:24.147
in like the fuckin'
background and something,

00:21:24.147 --> 00:21:25.530
and I'm just like, "Oh, okay, it's-"

00:21:25.530 --> 00:21:26.700
- Yeah, just ignore 'em. It's whatever.

00:21:26.700 --> 00:21:30.087
- Passionate anime fans, I've
heard it all before, you know?

00:21:30.087 --> 00:21:32.880
And then suddenly I see some guy

00:21:32.880 --> 00:21:35.042
just walking up to the
stage, and I'm just like,

00:21:35.042 --> 00:21:37.116
"Is this happening?"

00:21:37.116 --> 00:21:37.951
- Yeah.

00:21:37.951 --> 00:21:38.808
- Is this happening?

00:21:38.808 --> 00:21:41.070
- I heard like a guy go,
"No, no I'm coming on."

00:21:41.070 --> 00:21:42.357
And I was just like, "What?"

00:21:42.357 --> 00:21:44.299
And then, someone stood
up, and I was like,

00:21:44.299 --> 00:21:45.990
"What the fuck? Someone's coming up."

00:21:45.990 --> 00:21:46.890
- Yeah, yeah.

00:21:46.890 --> 00:21:47.790
- And I was like, "Oh no worries,

00:21:47.790 --> 00:21:48.930
security will deal with it."

00:21:48.930 --> 00:21:50.190
- Yeah. (laughing)

00:21:50.190 --> 00:21:51.720
- Yeah, it was like,
"There'll be someone there."

00:21:51.720 --> 00:21:52.553
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:21:52.553 --> 00:21:54.900
I was just like, "Okay,
he'll get to the stage.

00:21:54.900 --> 00:21:57.390
Oh no, he's on the stage.
Well, he'll get near the sofa.

00:21:57.390 --> 00:21:58.223
Oh no, he's near the sofa.

00:21:58.223 --> 00:22:00.330
Oh, oh, he's sitting next to Joey."

00:22:00.330 --> 00:22:03.240
And then I remember just like just waiting

00:22:03.240 --> 00:22:06.660
because I assumed that
there would be someone

00:22:06.660 --> 00:22:07.493
who would've come on and-

00:22:07.493 --> 00:22:09.346
- I mean, like someone's
coming from backstage.

00:22:09.346 --> 00:22:10.860
He's gonna come and collect him.

00:22:10.860 --> 00:22:11.910
- I was like, "Backstage?"

00:22:11.910 --> 00:22:14.820
No, I was like, "No, no one on the sides.

00:22:14.820 --> 00:22:17.790
Um, what did we do?"
- And a good like 30,

00:22:17.790 --> 00:22:21.630
40 seconds passed where nothing happened.

00:22:21.630 --> 00:22:24.690
- Even the crowd was
like, "Is this a bit?"

00:22:24.690 --> 00:22:26.190
Like, "What's happening?"

00:22:26.190 --> 00:22:28.470
- Yeah, it was so like out of left field

00:22:28.470 --> 00:22:30.630
that I talked to some
people, and originally,

00:22:30.630 --> 00:22:32.640
they thought that it
was just a special guest

00:22:32.640 --> 00:22:33.930
that had come on.

00:22:33.930 --> 00:22:34.988
- A special guest. (chuckles)
(Garnt and Connor laughing)

00:22:34.988 --> 00:22:37.899
- A special guest.

00:22:37.899 --> 00:22:38.732
- Just a random dude, yeah.

00:22:38.732 --> 00:22:42.330
- Yeah, just a bit in like
our show or something.

00:22:42.330 --> 00:22:44.430
And we were just like,

00:22:44.430 --> 00:22:46.200
I think the best way
to describe it is just,

00:22:46.200 --> 00:22:48.162
we were just shell shocked.

00:22:48.162 --> 00:22:48.995
- Yeah.

00:22:48.995 --> 00:22:52.067
I mean, it was definitely
traumatizing, that's for sure.

00:22:52.067 --> 00:22:55.500
'Cause that's like, yeah, as
I said, it was unprecedented.

00:22:55.500 --> 00:22:57.243
Like that's never happened at any,

00:22:57.243 --> 00:22:58.877
probably never any of our panels, right?

00:22:58.877 --> 00:22:59.790
- [Garnt and Connor] Yeah.

00:22:59.790 --> 00:23:01.050
- [Joey] Yeah, so it's just like-

00:23:01.050 --> 00:23:03.780
- I dunno how calm we looked on camera,

00:23:03.780 --> 00:23:05.730
but I'm pretty sure
internally, we were freaking

00:23:05.730 --> 00:23:06.960
the fuck out.
- Oh, I was shitting myself.

00:23:06.960 --> 00:23:07.890
'Cause I was like...

00:23:07.890 --> 00:23:09.690
This dude like sat right next to me,

00:23:09.690 --> 00:23:12.060
like he kinda like shoved me
outta the way 'cause I sitting

00:23:12.060 --> 00:23:13.547
kind of in the middle
of the couch like this,

00:23:13.547 --> 00:23:15.270
and he like shoved me out of the way.

00:23:15.270 --> 00:23:17.730
And then, he like, I mean,
everyone who was there saw it,

00:23:17.730 --> 00:23:19.620
but he tried to like
grab the mic off my hand.

00:23:19.620 --> 00:23:20.453
- I saw that.
- Yeah, 'cause he wanted

00:23:20.453 --> 00:23:22.230
to say something, and I
was like, "Ah, no, dude,"

00:23:22.230 --> 00:23:24.047
like, "What the fuck are you doing?"

00:23:24.047 --> 00:23:25.340
And then, yeah,

00:23:25.340 --> 00:23:27.630
he just like starts rambling
off about something,

00:23:27.630 --> 00:23:28.590
I don't even what the fuck.
- But he wasn't even

00:23:28.590 --> 00:23:29.858
like being coherent.

00:23:29.858 --> 00:23:32.425
- No, but it was just
like coming into one ear

00:23:32.425 --> 00:23:33.258
and out the other

00:23:33.258 --> 00:23:34.627
'cause I was just fuckin'
looking around like,

00:23:34.627 --> 00:23:36.850
"Ah, is anyone gonna do
anything about this?"

00:23:36.850 --> 00:23:38.250
- [Garnt] Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:23:38.250 --> 00:23:40.860
Like I remember what he was
talking about was nothing to do

00:23:40.860 --> 00:23:42.270
with what the question was asked

00:23:42.270 --> 00:23:43.470
or what we were talking about before.

00:23:43.470 --> 00:23:44.303
- He was just completely out of his mind.

00:23:44.303 --> 00:23:46.230
- He was just rambling on

00:23:46.230 --> 00:23:48.900
about something completely incoherent.

00:23:48.900 --> 00:23:52.410
And meanwhile, Joey is
frantically looking around,

00:23:52.410 --> 00:23:53.280
trying to find-

00:23:53.280 --> 00:23:55.530
- Joey, (chuckles) I
felt really bad for you.

00:23:55.530 --> 00:23:57.630
You were like, "Anyone? Anyone?"

00:23:57.630 --> 00:23:58.463
- I was like, "Help."

00:23:58.463 --> 00:24:01.080
Because I didn't wanna be the one

00:24:01.080 --> 00:24:02.220
to like instigate something.

00:24:02.220 --> 00:24:04.887
'Cause I don't know, the dude
might have a knife, you know?

00:24:04.887 --> 00:24:06.870
The dude might suddenly
fuckin' swing at me.

00:24:06.870 --> 00:24:08.783
So it's like, "I don't know what to do."

00:24:08.783 --> 00:24:10.823
I can't like push him off or anything

00:24:10.823 --> 00:24:11.880
'cause he was also fuckin' massive.

00:24:11.880 --> 00:24:12.960
- Yeah, this guy was big.

00:24:12.960 --> 00:24:14.160
- Yeah, big guy.

00:24:14.160 --> 00:24:18.450
- I mean, I not saying that I would punch

00:24:18.450 --> 00:24:20.580
if like a fuckin' two-foot
man came on the stage,

00:24:20.580 --> 00:24:23.370
but like I'd be a lot more
lightly just to be like,

00:24:23.370 --> 00:24:24.240
to try and leverage
(Garnt laughing)

00:24:24.240 --> 00:24:26.060
my own position if they were-

00:24:26.060 --> 00:24:28.145
- If a child comes onto
stage, you're like,

00:24:28.145 --> 00:24:29.347
"Okay, baby."
- Just stand up

00:24:29.347 --> 00:24:30.180
for the drop, kid.

00:24:30.180 --> 00:24:31.397
- Yeah. (laughing)

00:24:31.397 --> 00:24:33.630
- Well, it was just like,
you're in the situation,

00:24:33.630 --> 00:24:37.387
someone comes up, and you
look at him, and you're like,

00:24:37.387 --> 00:24:40.230
"If this guy really wanted
to swing for any of us,

00:24:40.230 --> 00:24:43.500
odds are it's gonna fuckin'
like really fuckin' hurt. "

00:24:43.500 --> 00:24:46.203
And I probably wouldn't
be able to punch him.

00:24:46.203 --> 00:24:49.200
Like he was really tall and big.

00:24:49.200 --> 00:24:51.060
So it's just like, you just sit there,

00:24:51.060 --> 00:24:52.260
and you're like weighing your odds.

00:24:52.260 --> 00:24:53.490
You're like, "What do I need to do?

00:24:53.490 --> 00:24:54.323
What's the best way to handle this?"

00:24:54.323 --> 00:24:56.280
Like I'm processing,
processing, processing.

00:24:56.280 --> 00:24:58.380
- Yeah, 'cause you rarely find yourself

00:24:58.380 --> 00:24:59.730
in a situation like this

00:24:59.730 --> 00:25:02.730
where you don't know what
the outcome is going to be,

00:25:02.730 --> 00:25:04.027
so in your head you are just like,

00:25:04.027 --> 00:25:06.060
"What's the worst outcome
this could possibly be

00:25:06.060 --> 00:25:07.604
and how could I prepare for it?"

00:25:07.604 --> 00:25:09.540
'Cause you're kind of in
like fight or flight mode

00:25:09.540 --> 00:25:10.800
at that point, right?

00:25:10.800 --> 00:25:12.061
- Yeah, and also, it's like,

00:25:12.061 --> 00:25:14.160
there was that like side of me as well

00:25:14.160 --> 00:25:15.810
that was like, okay, say for example,

00:25:15.810 --> 00:25:17.370
like if I fuckin' tripped him up

00:25:17.370 --> 00:25:19.380
as he was like trying to flee,

00:25:19.380 --> 00:25:20.850
and he like smashes his head in,

00:25:20.850 --> 00:25:22.080
and he's gonna Amber Heard me

00:25:22.080 --> 00:25:25.426
and like try and sue me
for defamation and damages.

00:25:25.426 --> 00:25:26.259
(Garnt laughing)

00:25:26.259 --> 00:25:27.092
I was like, "I didn't want that either."

00:25:27.092 --> 00:25:30.030
So it's like, I literally
couldn't do anything,

00:25:30.030 --> 00:25:32.100
and I just had to sit there and be like,

00:25:32.100 --> 00:25:34.140
just prayge that way
someone would help me.

00:25:34.140 --> 00:25:36.343
- I was just like hoping, I was, "Okay."

00:25:36.343 --> 00:25:37.747
Obviously, a lot of people were like,

00:25:37.747 --> 00:25:39.510
"Man, you should've just like
punched him or something,"

00:25:39.510 --> 00:25:41.050
and it's like, "Well, it's like,

00:25:41.050 --> 00:25:43.880
I don't wanna be the one to escalate it."

00:25:43.880 --> 00:25:45.240
At the end of the day,
we're still on stage,

00:25:45.240 --> 00:25:46.073
and we are trying-

00:25:46.073 --> 00:25:47.190
- Bro, Creator Clash was like a month ago.

