01:09:22.599 --> 01:09:24.810
And so we're with him for
half an hour to 45 minutes,

01:09:24.810 --> 01:09:28.860
and then I go into the toilet quickly,

01:09:28.860 --> 01:09:30.930
and then as I come outside,

01:09:30.930 --> 01:09:32.640
apparently when I was in the toilets,

01:09:32.640 --> 01:09:34.560
this mythical sister comes.

01:09:34.560 --> 01:09:35.393
And she's just like,

01:09:35.393 --> 01:09:36.930
"Oh, thank you so much for
taking care of my brother.

01:09:36.930 --> 01:09:39.480
I'm so sorry. I dunno what's
happened to his mates.

01:09:39.480 --> 01:09:41.370
I dunno what's happened to him.

01:09:41.370 --> 01:09:42.987
I'll make sure he gets home okay."

01:09:42.987 --> 01:09:44.550
And then like the next line,

01:09:44.550 --> 01:09:45.820
which is the line I heard

01:09:45.820 --> 01:09:50.820
as I was walking out the
door to go outside again was,

01:09:51.547 --> 01:09:53.610
"By the way, did you guys
see the Trash Taste boys

01:09:53.610 --> 01:09:55.980
in MCM today?
(all laughing)

01:09:55.980 --> 01:09:57.054
- What, the sister said this?

01:09:57.054 --> 01:09:59.388
- Yeah, yeah, yeah, the
sister said this, right.

01:09:59.388 --> 01:10:00.221
- [Joey] Oh my God.

01:10:00.221 --> 01:10:03.960
- My mates told me it was
like sitcom level timing.

01:10:03.960 --> 01:10:05.040
She was like so compassionate.

01:10:05.040 --> 01:10:06.810
And then she was just
trying to make conversation.

01:10:06.810 --> 01:10:09.337
And then, she just mentioned,

01:10:09.337 --> 01:10:11.130
"Did you guys manage to
see the Trash Taste boys?"

01:10:11.130 --> 01:10:12.315
- And then, what?

01:10:12.315 --> 01:10:14.051
You just like slowly back inside, right?

01:10:14.051 --> 01:10:17.340
- No, no, and then the
automatic doors open.

01:10:17.340 --> 01:10:19.853
And then everyone looks
at me, and she just goes,

01:10:19.853 --> 01:10:24.853
"No, no! You?!"
(Joey and Connor laughing)

01:10:24.900 --> 01:10:26.580
- But you were on the
phone with her, right?

01:10:26.580 --> 01:10:30.677
- No, I wasn't on the phone with here.

01:10:30.677 --> 01:10:33.120
It was someone else on the
phone, but they had mentioned

01:10:33.120 --> 01:10:37.879
that we had a bunch of guys
taking care of her brother.

01:10:37.879 --> 01:10:39.690
I was like the guy who was
just like chatting to him,

01:10:39.690 --> 01:10:41.220
trying to make sure,

01:10:41.220 --> 01:10:42.870
trying to know what the
fuck happened to him tonight

01:10:42.870 --> 01:10:44.521
and make sure he felt
comfortable and that shit.

01:10:44.521 --> 01:10:47.310
And she was just like, "You
were taking care of him?!"

01:10:47.310 --> 01:10:49.920
You!? You?!" (laughing)

01:10:49.920 --> 01:10:51.960
And I was just like, "Are you the sister?

01:10:51.960 --> 01:10:54.930
Are you the mythical sister?"
And she's like, "Yes."

01:10:54.930 --> 01:10:57.521
And I was like, first I said,

01:10:57.521 --> 01:11:00.570
"Thank you so much for being amazing."

01:11:00.570 --> 01:11:01.890
I could tell like she was like

01:11:01.890 --> 01:11:03.750
trying to hold in her excitement.

01:11:03.750 --> 01:11:07.350
And then, she pauses for a second.

01:11:07.350 --> 01:11:09.720
She looks at her brother,
dead on the floor.

01:11:09.720 --> 01:11:10.957
And she's like,

01:11:10.957 --> 01:11:13.290
"I know this is a bad time,
(Joey and Connor laughing)

01:11:13.290 --> 01:11:15.123
but is it cool if I ask for a picture?"

01:11:15.123 --> 01:11:16.343
(all laughing)

01:11:16.343 --> 01:11:20.928
- No, no! It doesn't
even sound real, dude.

01:11:20.928 --> 01:11:23.347
- 100% it happened, and I'm just like,

01:11:23.347 --> 01:11:25.590
"Look, you were like such a gigachad

01:11:25.590 --> 01:11:28.263
for coming all the way
out here, like 1:00 AM.

01:11:28.263 --> 01:11:31.109
Luckily, we had other people
to take care of her brother.

01:11:31.109 --> 01:11:32.490
(Garnt laughing)

01:11:32.490 --> 01:11:35.910
We take a quick picture, she
goes home, and everyone's safe.

01:11:35.910 --> 01:11:36.743
Everyone's safe.

01:11:36.743 --> 01:11:38.370
- Please tell me the
brother was in the shot.

01:11:38.370 --> 01:11:40.270
Like in the background.
(Garnt laughing)

01:11:40.270 --> 01:11:41.940
It's like that mean picture of the guy

01:11:41.940 --> 01:11:44.432
like leaning towards the
grave and like doing that.

01:11:44.432 --> 01:11:45.265
(all laughing)

01:11:45.265 --> 01:11:46.176
Except it's like

01:11:46.176 --> 01:11:48.531
the brother's just like
dead on the floor, like.

01:11:48.531 --> 01:11:49.653
(all laughing)

01:11:49.653 --> 01:11:51.000
- That doesn't even sound real.

01:11:51.000 --> 01:11:54.148
Like it sounds so like in between his ass.

01:11:54.148 --> 01:11:56.125
- It does, it was like so surreal.

01:11:56.125 --> 01:11:56.958
- [Joey] That's so funny.

01:11:56.958 --> 01:11:59.574
One of the funniest things that
happened to me that weekend.

01:11:59.574 --> 01:12:00.407
(Joey laughing)

01:12:00.407 --> 01:12:01.620
But yes, it's just like,

01:12:01.620 --> 01:12:05.520
sometimes you just have like
really weird coincidences

01:12:05.520 --> 01:12:07.560
and weird timings with shit, man.

01:12:07.560 --> 01:12:10.470
- That is like the words you
must never utter at a con.

01:12:10.470 --> 01:12:13.110
Of like, huh, what if? Hilarious, right?

01:12:13.110 --> 01:12:14.790
And then almost every single time,

01:12:14.790 --> 01:12:16.950
it's like, "Oh, hi," from a distance.

01:12:16.950 --> 01:12:17.898
- Yeah, right.

01:12:17.898 --> 01:12:19.720
- Fuck's sake. Where's the canned laugh?

01:12:19.720 --> 01:12:24.720
- Yeah, yeah, yeah. Where's
the live audience? (laughs)

01:12:25.680 --> 01:12:26.580
- Oh my God.

01:12:26.580 --> 01:12:28.067
- Aside from MCM, though,

01:12:28.067 --> 01:12:31.410
how is your guys experience
being back in the UK now?

01:12:31.410 --> 01:12:32.243
This is your second time-
- Good, good.

01:12:32.243 --> 01:12:33.330
- in the UK.

01:12:33.330 --> 01:12:34.260
- Only my second time, yeah.

01:12:34.260 --> 01:12:35.730
- I dunno if you had a lot of chance

01:12:35.730 --> 01:12:37.227
to explore England outside of-

01:12:37.227 --> 01:12:39.304
- No, we've been in...

01:12:39.304 --> 01:12:41.610
'Cause the MCM in London
is kind of outta the way,

01:12:41.610 --> 01:12:44.340
so we've kind of been just
kind of contained there.

01:12:44.340 --> 01:12:46.080
- And like the first time I was around,

01:12:46.080 --> 01:12:50.230
I think in like 2017,
2018, whenever it was,

01:12:50.230 --> 01:12:52.440
I was mostly in Brighton at Garnt's place.

01:12:52.440 --> 01:12:57.440
So I think I was only in London
for maybe like a day or so.

01:12:57.479 --> 01:12:59.996
I think this will be
like my first proper time

01:12:59.996 --> 01:13:01.500
kind of like getting to check it out.

01:13:01.500 --> 01:13:03.420
And I've already seen way more of London

01:13:03.420 --> 01:13:04.530
than I ever did last time,

01:13:04.530 --> 01:13:06.660
so, yeah it's been, it's been chill.

01:13:06.660 --> 01:13:09.630
I mean the weather's been
fantastic this weekend as well,

01:13:09.630 --> 01:13:10.679
which is great.

01:13:10.679 --> 01:13:11.880
'Cause like everyone was like, "Oh yeah,"

01:13:11.880 --> 01:13:12.907
when I tweeted about like,

01:13:12.907 --> 01:13:14.910
"Oh yeah, I'm landing in London soon.

01:13:14.910 --> 01:13:16.020
Haha, it's gonna be sick."

01:13:16.020 --> 01:13:18.817
And everyone was just like,
"Weather's gonna be shit."

01:13:18.817 --> 01:13:19.987
"Shit weather,

01:13:19.987 --> 01:13:21.090
"Expect the shit weather."
- It's been good.

01:13:21.090 --> 01:13:21.923
It's really good.

01:13:21.923 --> 01:13:23.940
- Yeah, and I landed, and I was just like-

01:13:23.940 --> 01:13:25.035
- Brought the red carpet.
- What the fuck?

01:13:25.035 --> 01:13:27.057
This is shit weather, you guys?!

01:13:27.057 --> 01:13:29.220
- Literally, I remember the
first day meeting you all.

01:13:29.220 --> 01:13:31.250
It was like, you couldn't
ask for like better weather.

01:13:31.250 --> 01:13:32.970
It was literally clear skies.

01:13:32.970 --> 01:13:34.773
It was clear blue skies.
- Yeah, it was like warm,

01:13:34.773 --> 01:13:38.340
like not too hot, like
nice and toasty, bright.

01:13:38.340 --> 01:13:39.660
You know, perfect, sunglasses.

01:13:39.660 --> 01:13:42.450
Like having a coffee
outside type of weather.

01:13:42.450 --> 01:13:44.675
And everyone was like, "Yeah,
shit weather, shit weather."

01:13:44.675 --> 01:13:46.680
- I was like, "Oh man, you
guys got it good here."

01:13:46.680 --> 01:13:48.510
Apparently though, it was
just like an absolute fluke.

01:13:48.510 --> 01:13:50.193
Like everyone was like,
"Damn, this is fucked.

01:13:50.193 --> 01:13:52.668
It's actually good weather here. Jesus."

01:13:52.668 --> 01:13:54.257
- I think around this time
of year it's okay, though.

01:13:54.257 --> 01:13:55.380
- This is a pretty good time

01:13:55.380 --> 01:13:56.490
to come to London.
- Because the last time

01:13:56.490 --> 01:13:57.323
I was in the UK,

01:13:57.323 --> 01:13:59.872
it was like the biggest
heat wave in like 30 years

01:13:59.872 --> 01:14:00.705
or whatever it was.
- That's like every year.

01:14:00.705 --> 01:14:03.287
It's the biggest heat
wave every fuckin' year.

01:14:03.287 --> 01:14:05.400
- We get one week, or in your case,

01:14:05.400 --> 01:14:07.950
it was like the one month of just-

01:14:07.950 --> 01:14:08.950
- That was really fuckin'
hot that time you came.

01:14:08.950 --> 01:14:10.380
- Yeah, like holy shit.
- I remember that time.

01:14:10.380 --> 01:14:11.910
- Like the heat wave in the UK,

01:14:11.910 --> 01:14:13.619
just we are not built for it.

01:14:13.619 --> 01:14:14.472
- And I was just like, "Where's the AC?"

01:14:14.472 --> 01:14:15.305
(Garnt chuckling)

01:14:15.305 --> 01:14:16.138
"Where's the AC?"

01:14:16.138 --> 01:14:17.370
- We don't have any.

01:14:17.370 --> 01:14:18.510
- [Garnt and Joey] Yeah.

01:14:18.510 --> 01:14:20.160
- I mean, yeah, it's been good so far.

01:14:20.160 --> 01:14:21.990
I haven't really done anything. Oh God.

01:14:21.990 --> 01:14:25.517
Dude, I haven't really awkward
interaction at the hotel.

01:14:25.517 --> 01:14:28.487
It was really like (gasping)

01:14:28.487 --> 01:14:30.381
That was of an awkwardness.
- Which one?

01:14:30.381 --> 01:14:31.800
(Connor gasping)

01:14:31.800 --> 01:14:34.590
- Well, so we were in the hotel bar

01:14:34.590 --> 01:14:36.600
just talking to all our friends.

01:14:36.600 --> 01:14:38.340
'Cause it's the Sunday,
it's after the cons end,

01:14:38.340 --> 01:14:39.210
and everyone's just chilling.

01:14:39.210 --> 01:14:40.320
We're all just hanging out,

01:14:40.320 --> 01:14:41.610
saying goodbye to all our friends.

01:14:41.610 --> 01:14:44.460
And this person was like
pretty chill at first.

01:14:44.460 --> 01:14:45.727
And like they would kind
come up and be like,

01:14:45.727 --> 01:14:47.610
"Oh, hi, do you wanna drink or anything?"

01:14:47.610 --> 01:14:49.260
And I was like, "Oh no,
it's okay, it's okay."

01:14:49.260 --> 01:14:51.560
And I got my friend to
buy me a drink instead.

01:14:52.467 --> 01:14:53.753
I didn't that their money.

01:14:53.753 --> 01:14:56.460
(all laughing)

01:14:56.460 --> 01:14:59.610
And then, they were kinda
like, just kept saying hi,

01:14:59.610 --> 01:15:00.443
which is fine.

01:15:00.443 --> 01:15:02.460
Like it's chill, 'cause
people do it all the time,

01:15:02.460 --> 01:15:03.293
and it's like, whatever.

01:15:03.293 --> 01:15:05.186
- Yeah, probably a couple of
drinks deep at that point?

01:15:05.186 --> 01:15:06.210
- Yeah, yeah.

01:15:06.210 --> 01:15:08.670
If someone's having a bunch of drinks

01:15:08.670 --> 01:15:09.927
and enjoying themselves,
they wanna be like,

01:15:09.927 --> 01:15:11.673
"Oh my God. Yeah, hi, you're there."

01:15:11.673 --> 01:15:14.070
It's like, whatever. I don't mind that.

01:15:14.070 --> 01:15:15.780
But I noticed that like
whenever we would like...

01:15:15.780 --> 01:15:18.750
If I went outside or like
any of you guys went outside,

01:15:18.750 --> 01:15:21.364
they would like kind of like
also then happen to go outside

01:15:21.364 --> 01:15:22.800
at the same time

01:15:22.800 --> 01:15:25.290
and just listen to whatever
you're talking about.

01:15:25.290 --> 01:15:27.989
And then, you know, I'd go
to the toilet, then suddenly,

01:15:27.989 --> 01:15:29.100
they were in the toilet as well.

01:15:29.100 --> 01:15:30.117
And I was like, "Okay, this is like,"

01:15:30.117 --> 01:15:32.550
all right, a little sauce,
but like nothing happened.

01:15:32.550 --> 01:15:34.470
So I was like, "All right,
cool, cool, cool. It's chill."

01:15:34.470 --> 01:15:35.430
- It's kinda like tailgating
a little bit, right?

01:15:35.430 --> 01:15:37.680
- Yeah, it just kinda
like watching, I guess,

01:15:37.680 --> 01:15:39.990
which is, obviously, it's like not ideal,

01:15:39.990 --> 01:15:41.220
but it's nothing bad.

01:15:41.220 --> 01:15:43.200
It's like I'm more like,
"All right, whatever."

01:15:43.200 --> 01:15:44.970
But then like you guys went to bed,

01:15:44.970 --> 01:15:46.520
and there was only maybe
like six of us left.

01:15:46.520 --> 01:15:47.370
We were chilling.

01:15:48.430 --> 01:15:50.970
And there was like two couches,

01:15:50.970 --> 01:15:52.860
and there's like an empty space

01:15:52.860 --> 01:15:55.170
because obviously, you guys
had gone to bed and stuff.

01:15:55.170 --> 01:15:56.227
And they came over, and they were like,

01:15:56.227 --> 01:15:58.723
"Hey, do you mind if
I like take the seat?"

01:15:58.723 --> 01:16:00.510
It was like 1:00 AM, so
it's kind of winding down.

01:16:00.510 --> 01:16:01.343
And I was like,

01:16:01.343 --> 01:16:03.330
"Yeah, I don't really
think that's appropriate

01:16:03.330 --> 01:16:04.470
'cause like no one really knows you.

01:16:04.470 --> 01:16:05.370
You don't really know me.

01:16:05.370 --> 01:16:07.410
And like, you know, it's
kinda weird and stuff."

01:16:07.410 --> 01:16:10.350
And they were like, "Oh, oh, okay.

01:16:10.350 --> 01:16:12.000
Well, do you mind if I
just introduce myself

01:16:12.000 --> 01:16:13.392
to everyone then?"
- No.

01:16:13.392 --> 01:16:15.817
- And I was like (inhales deeply)

01:16:15.817 --> 01:16:18.663
"Yeah, no, I don't think
that's like the best.

01:16:19.950 --> 01:16:22.110
I appreciate it, but like, no,

01:16:22.110 --> 01:16:23.430
it makes this a bit uncomfortable.

01:16:23.430 --> 01:16:24.300
- So the doing intention is there,

01:16:24.300 --> 01:16:26.250
but they clearly didn't
quite read the room-

01:16:26.250 --> 01:16:28.650
- Yeah, I was trying to be as like polite,

01:16:28.650 --> 01:16:31.050
but like no as possible.

01:16:31.050 --> 01:16:32.160
'Cause like at the end of the day,

01:16:32.160 --> 01:16:33.983
like there's still
somebody who, even though,

01:16:33.983 --> 01:16:35.133
I guess some people would be like,

01:16:35.133 --> 01:16:36.900
"No, you have the promotion
to be like 'fuck off'

01:16:36.900 --> 01:16:37.740
at that point."

01:16:37.740 --> 01:16:38.737
'Cause people say that, and I'm like,

01:16:38.737 --> 01:16:40.380
"I still don't wanna do that."

01:16:40.380 --> 01:16:42.120
Like to me, it's like,
"There's still a person."

01:16:42.120 --> 01:16:43.020
- I don't wanna be that guy, right?

01:16:43.020 --> 01:16:44.940
- They shoot at their
shot, and it didn't work.

01:16:44.940 --> 01:16:47.340
And they should've just
given up at that point.

01:16:47.340 --> 01:16:49.297
But then, after I said
that again, I was like,

01:16:49.297 --> 01:16:50.527
"No, I don't think that's..."

01:16:50.527 --> 01:16:51.690
"Come on, man, like no,"

01:16:51.690 --> 01:16:54.420
They just kinda like
stood there awkwardly,

01:16:54.420 --> 01:16:56.616
just like looking at us. (chuckles)

01:16:56.616 --> 01:16:58.560
And then, it was just kinda like,

01:16:58.560 --> 01:17:00.750
all my friends were
just looking at me like,

01:17:00.750 --> 01:17:01.583
and I was like, "Yeah."

01:17:01.583 --> 01:17:02.513
- Like "Yeah, please do something."

01:17:02.513 --> 01:17:06.690
- I'm like, "Okay, all right, man, bye."

01:17:06.690 --> 01:17:09.808
Wouldn't leave, and then one
of our friends just goes,

01:17:09.808 --> 01:17:10.770
(Connor laughing)

01:17:10.770 --> 01:17:12.690
What the fuck did he say?

01:17:12.690 --> 01:17:14.520
He was like, "Just please leave us alone."

01:17:14.520 --> 01:17:15.420
(all laughing)

01:17:15.420 --> 01:17:17.820
Like he was begging in
like a pleading way.

01:17:17.820 --> 01:17:19.410
It was like, "Please just leave us alone."

01:17:19.410 --> 01:17:20.243
- Please!

01:17:20.243 --> 01:17:21.076
- Please, just leave us alone.

01:17:21.076 --> 01:17:23.837
- I think I know who. I think
I can guess who the guy is.

01:17:23.837 --> 01:17:27.234
- It was such a like desperate
way that the person was like,

01:17:27.234 --> 01:17:28.998
"Yeah, yeah, sorry,
sorry, sorry." (laughing)

01:17:28.998 --> 01:17:31.770
I was just like, "Oh no,"

01:17:31.770 --> 01:17:34.050
but that was really funny
the way he said that.

01:17:34.050 --> 01:17:34.883
(Garnt laughing)
It was really.

01:17:34.883 --> 01:17:35.900
- Please, leave us alone.

01:17:35.900 --> 01:17:36.963
- Please, leave us alone.

01:17:36.963 --> 01:17:37.796
(Joey whining)

01:17:37.796 --> 01:17:38.873
- Yeah.

01:17:38.873 --> 01:17:42.030
I mean, when you hang out at
the bar at the convention,

01:17:42.030 --> 01:17:44.520
in the convention hotel,
this shit is gonna happen.

01:17:44.520 --> 01:17:46.410
Like if we really wanted
to go somewhere else

01:17:46.410 --> 01:17:49.080
and like avoid this shit, we could've.

01:17:49.080 --> 01:17:51.240
But like we just wanted the convenience.

01:17:51.240 --> 01:17:53.670
We were all staying in
that hotel. It's chill.

01:17:53.670 --> 01:17:55.217
So like when people do shit like that,

01:17:55.217 --> 01:17:56.527
I know people get like,

01:17:56.527 --> 01:17:57.781
"That's fucked up that they did that."

01:17:57.781 --> 01:17:58.950
I'm like, "Yeah, it's not ideal."

01:17:58.950 --> 01:18:00.517
But I'm also like, you know,

01:18:00.517 --> 01:18:02.190
"People get excited,
they shoot their shot.

01:18:02.190 --> 01:18:03.090
They didn't do anything.

01:18:03.090 --> 01:18:05.297
They asked. They didn't just sit down."

01:18:05.297 --> 01:18:06.870
'Cause people have done that before.

01:18:06.870 --> 01:18:08.730
People just fuckin' pull and grab.

01:18:08.730 --> 01:18:11.245
- Yeah, but we've been good.
- On the panel, for instance.

01:18:11.245 --> 01:18:14.250
- See, I'm glad people can now know

01:18:14.250 --> 01:18:15.454
that we aren't bullshitting.

01:18:15.454 --> 01:18:17.550
- No, like you can...

01:18:17.550 --> 01:18:20.227
You have the right, anyone
has the right to be like,

01:18:20.227 --> 01:18:21.310
"Hey, can I join you?"

01:18:21.310 --> 01:18:22.537
And I have the right to say,

01:18:22.537 --> 01:18:24.930
"No, fuck off."
- Yeah, exactly.

01:18:24.930 --> 01:18:25.763
- You know what I mean?

01:18:25.763 --> 01:18:26.910
Like I'm not gonna get at someone

01:18:26.910 --> 01:18:28.110
for trying to shoot their shot.

01:18:28.110 --> 01:18:29.910
And if you want to, whatever.

01:18:29.910 --> 01:18:32.460
Is it kind of rude and
insensitive to do it? Yeah, it is.

01:18:32.460 --> 01:18:33.496
But at the same time-

01:18:33.496 --> 01:18:35.220
- But at same time,
like respect my privacy.

01:18:35.220 --> 01:18:36.053
- Yeah.

01:18:36.053 --> 01:18:36.886
If you did it respectfully,

01:18:36.886 --> 01:18:38.430
I'm gonna give you the respect to be like,

01:18:38.430 --> 01:18:41.790
explain it nicely and be like,
"That's not appropriate, no."

01:18:41.790 --> 01:18:42.720
And if you don't get it,

01:18:42.720 --> 01:18:45.810
then (chuckles) maybe one of
my friends won't be so nice.

01:18:45.810 --> 01:18:47.860
But I'll still be nice, but I don't know.

01:18:48.810 --> 01:18:50.159
- Please just leave alone.

01:18:50.159 --> 01:18:51.193
(Garnt laughing)

01:18:51.193 --> 01:18:54.167
- Yeah, I dunno.

01:18:54.167 --> 01:18:56.580
I just say these stories
'cause it's on my mind,

01:18:56.580 --> 01:18:57.480
wanted to talk about it,

01:18:57.480 --> 01:18:59.160
but I know it's gonna happen again.

01:18:59.160 --> 01:19:01.410
It's not gonna be the last time.

01:19:01.410 --> 01:19:04.710
If you ever see me around,
and you ask to sit next to me,

01:19:04.710 --> 01:19:06.657
I'm probably gonna say no 99...

01:19:06.657 --> 01:19:09.098
No, fuck it, I am gonna say no 99-

01:19:09.098 --> 01:19:10.181
- 100% of the time.

01:19:10.181 --> 01:19:11.160
- 100% of the time.

01:19:11.160 --> 01:19:13.230
- I'm gonna say no probably
'cause I don't know you,

01:19:13.230 --> 01:19:14.063
and it's weird.

01:19:14.940 --> 01:19:15.773
- Yeah, it's like-

01:19:15.773 --> 01:19:16.740
- It's not organic.

01:19:16.740 --> 01:19:17.573
- Yeah, yeah.

01:19:17.573 --> 01:19:20.340
I think in a convention setting,

01:19:20.340 --> 01:19:24.930
it's hard to like draw like
a comfortable line, you know?

01:19:24.930 --> 01:19:27.360
Whereas maybe if you
meet someone at a bar,

01:19:27.360 --> 01:19:29.040
and you're not with like
a massive group of friends

01:19:29.040 --> 01:19:29.873
or whatever-
- It's different.

01:19:29.873 --> 01:19:30.706
- it's different.

01:19:30.706 --> 01:19:31.898
- [Joey] Yeah, definitely different.

01:19:31.898 --> 01:19:33.540
- It's very different.

01:19:33.540 --> 01:19:36.150
It's you kind of do have to
like read the room sometimes,

01:19:36.150 --> 01:19:40.050
which I know some people
aren't as in tune with that

01:19:40.050 --> 01:19:40.883
as other people.

01:19:40.883 --> 01:19:42.960
But you try not to hold
things against people

01:19:42.960 --> 01:19:46.743
unless they like seriously do
cross like a social boundary,

01:19:48.360 --> 01:19:49.193
in which case,

01:19:49.193 --> 01:19:50.697
maybe I should listen
to fuckin' Ditus more

01:19:50.697 --> 01:19:52.527
and just be like, "Sorry man."

01:19:54.351 --> 01:19:55.482
- Did you use the man technique?

01:19:55.482 --> 01:19:56.315
- Yeah, did you use the man-

01:19:56.315 --> 01:19:57.930
- I dunno, I think I just waffled on

01:19:57.930 --> 01:19:59.400
for 10 minutes
(Garnt laughing)

01:19:59.400 --> 01:20:01.170
Just being like, "No, no.

01:20:01.170 --> 01:20:04.506
Here's another reason why no.
Here's another reason why no.

01:20:04.506 --> 01:20:05.339
Here's another reason why."

01:20:05.339 --> 01:20:06.172
- If he would've just said, "Sorry, man,"

01:20:06.172 --> 01:20:07.685
then they would be like, "All
right, man, I respect that."

01:20:07.685 --> 01:20:09.210
- "I respect," that's
what we should've said

01:20:09.210 --> 01:20:10.740
to that guy who came on stage.

01:20:10.740 --> 01:20:12.510
Fuck, he was right all along!

01:20:12.510 --> 01:20:14.969
- I should've just turned
and being like, "Sorry man."

01:20:14.969 --> 01:20:17.197
(Joey and Garnt laughing)

01:20:17.197 --> 01:20:19.111
- "Sorry, man, this just
aint' the place, man."

01:20:19.111 --> 01:20:20.160
- [Joey] Oh, man.

01:20:20.160 --> 01:20:21.130
- There was this one dude,

01:20:21.130 --> 01:20:25.110
and I like (chuckles) still
don't know what his deal was.

01:20:25.110 --> 01:20:26.850
I was like, we were at the bar with John,

01:20:26.850 --> 01:20:28.267
and John was talking
to me, and I was like,

01:20:28.267 --> 01:20:30.450
"John, man, yeah, it sucks, dude."

01:20:30.450 --> 01:20:31.595
I was like, "Yeah, it kind sucks."

01:20:31.595 --> 01:20:32.580
- Super Eyepatch.
- Super Eyepatch.

01:20:32.580 --> 01:20:33.624
- Sorry, sorry.
(Garnt laughing)

01:20:33.624 --> 01:20:34.457
I did it, I did it.

01:20:34.457 --> 01:20:35.290
- You literally just did it!

01:20:35.290 --> 01:20:36.123
- I did it, I did it.

01:20:36.123 --> 01:20:37.080
- What did you tell Garnt before?

01:20:37.080 --> 01:20:38.910
- But we've said John like
a million times, right?

01:20:38.910 --> 01:20:39.899
I should've said Kevin too.
- It's just there's

01:20:39.899 --> 01:20:40.732
so many other John's.

01:20:40.732 --> 01:20:41.565
(Joey laughing)

01:20:41.565 --> 01:20:43.140
- Literally, such a common name.

01:20:43.140 --> 01:20:44.460
- I was in my own head, I'm sorry.

01:20:44.460 --> 01:20:47.190
Okay, that's my bad. I suck, dude.

01:20:47.190 --> 01:20:48.690
Yeah, I was telling Super Eyepatch Wolf,

01:20:48.690 --> 01:20:49.995
I was like, "Yeah, man, it sucks, dude.

01:20:49.995 --> 01:20:52.530
I don't feel like I can't
really like experience

01:20:52.530 --> 01:20:54.150
a con the way I used to."

01:20:54.150 --> 01:20:58.020
And then while (chuckles) I'm
telling this story to John,

01:20:58.020 --> 01:21:00.150
this guy who must have
been like 40 or 50ish

01:21:00.150 --> 01:21:02.850
just shouts full on from across the bar.

01:21:02.850 --> 01:21:06.480
He's like, "Hey, Connor,
Connor, you want a drink?

01:21:06.480 --> 01:21:07.313
You want a drink?"

01:21:07.313 --> 01:21:09.306
And I'm like, "Nah, I'm good man."

01:21:09.306 --> 01:21:10.650
And John was like, "You know that guy?"

01:21:10.650 --> 01:21:11.817
I'm like, "No fuckin' clue."

01:21:11.817 --> 01:21:15.210
(all laughing)

01:21:15.210 --> 01:21:18.840
I know, it's just like so weird.

01:21:18.840 --> 01:21:21.240
- I get it because that
happened to me a few times

01:21:21.240 --> 01:21:22.710
in other conventions.

01:21:22.710 --> 01:21:23.610
- He was nice enough.

01:21:23.610 --> 01:21:25.243
He just asked me, and I was like, "No."

01:21:25.243 --> 01:21:26.880
And that was it. That was it.

01:21:26.880 --> 01:21:30.360
- Because they shout your
name in such familiarity

01:21:30.360 --> 01:21:32.977
that even I have to
double take to be like,

01:21:32.977 --> 01:21:34.243
"Do I know this guy?"
- Yeah, yeah. (laughing)

01:21:34.243 --> 01:21:35.266
Do you know what I mean?
- Yeah. (laughing)

01:21:35.266 --> 01:21:36.920
Do you know what I mean? (laughing)

01:21:36.920 --> 01:21:39.480
'Cause like a few times
when I hang out with mates,

01:21:39.480 --> 01:21:41.547
like I will hear like,
"Garnt, hey, Garnt."

01:21:41.547 --> 01:21:43.370
And I'm just like, "Oh it's...

01:21:44.640 --> 01:21:47.100
Wait, I've never met this
man in my life." (laughs)

01:21:47.100 --> 01:21:48.150
- Yeah. (laughing)

01:21:48.150 --> 01:21:49.900
- It's like friend of a friend? No?

01:21:50.932 --> 01:21:51.870
Oh my God.

01:21:51.870 --> 01:21:52.777
- Don't offer me a drink.

01:21:52.777 --> 01:21:55.260
"I'm privileged," as you
all say, so don't fuckin'...

01:21:55.260 --> 01:21:56.430
I don't need it. I'm good.

01:21:56.430 --> 01:21:57.263
- He can buy his own drink.

01:21:57.263 --> 01:21:58.830
- I buy my own y'all, I promise.

01:21:58.830 --> 01:21:59.670
I appreciate it, though.

01:21:59.670 --> 01:22:02.250
Some people are just nice.

01:22:02.250 --> 01:22:04.213
I had one time I was
in London last time...

01:22:04.213 --> 01:22:05.046
I never told this.

01:22:05.046 --> 01:22:07.710
It was like someone in
like a Mexican restaurant.

01:22:07.710 --> 01:22:08.580
It was like the thing in the movie.

01:22:08.580 --> 01:22:09.666
It was like,

01:22:09.666 --> 01:22:10.953
"That person over there
wants to buy you a drink,"

01:22:10.953 --> 01:22:12.277
when the waiter came over, I was like,

01:22:12.277 --> 01:22:14.934
"This is fuckin' cool.
Yeah, I'll have it."

01:22:14.934 --> 01:22:17.221
(all laughing)

01:22:17.221 --> 01:22:20.130
He bought me like the strongest
drink on the fuckin' menu.

01:22:20.130 --> 01:22:22.320
And I was like (coughing)

01:22:22.320 --> 01:22:23.250
- It's like trying to spike you.

01:22:23.250 --> 01:22:24.386
- So then I realized, I was like,

01:22:24.386 --> 01:22:25.331
"Yeah, I'm not doing this again.

01:22:25.331 --> 01:22:27.900
I'm not letting them choose the drink."

01:22:27.900 --> 01:22:29.670
- The weirder one for me is like the ones

01:22:29.670 --> 01:22:31.530
where it's like just in passing,

01:22:31.530 --> 01:22:33.990
but you're also like not too sure either

01:22:33.990 --> 01:22:35.520
because the lack of information.

01:22:35.520 --> 01:22:36.900
Like it's the ones where you're like,

01:22:36.900 --> 01:22:38.070
where you're in the hotel lobby,

01:22:38.070 --> 01:22:39.960
and you're trying to get
to the toilet or something.

01:22:39.960 --> 01:22:41.790
And then a person is walking past you,

01:22:41.790 --> 01:22:44.700
and you just very
briefly have eye contact,

01:22:44.700 --> 01:22:48.690
and they just go.
(Garnt laughing)

01:22:48.690 --> 01:22:51.912
And then they walk off, and
I'm just like, "Do I know you?"

01:22:51.912 --> 01:22:53.700
(all laughing)

01:22:53.700 --> 01:22:55.913
- This is something like
"The Number 23" shit.

01:22:55.913 --> 01:22:56.940
It's just like, "Wake up."

01:22:56.940 --> 01:22:58.981
It's like, "Wake up." (chuckles)

01:22:58.981 --> 01:23:00.150
- That does happen a lot.

01:23:00.150 --> 01:23:01.110
- It does happen a lot.

01:23:01.110 --> 01:23:01.943
And I'm just like...

01:23:01.943 --> 01:23:04.050
And it's not until I turn around,

01:23:04.050 --> 01:23:06.007
and sometimes, they'll
turn around and be like,

01:23:06.007 --> 01:23:07.080
"Hey, love you stuff,"

01:23:07.080 --> 01:23:08.730
or like, "Hope you're
having a good night,"

01:23:08.730 --> 01:23:09.702
and stuff like that."

01:23:09.702 --> 01:23:11.160
You know, maybe they're just
being friendly. I don't know.

01:23:11.160 --> 01:23:14.160
But it's like, it's just the silent nod.

01:23:14.160 --> 01:23:16.818
Like, what? Is this code
for something? (chuckles)

01:23:16.818 --> 01:23:19.380
Yeah, but it's cool, though.
(Connor burps)

01:23:19.380 --> 01:23:20.340
- Sorry.

01:23:20.340 --> 01:23:21.173
- It's cool.

01:23:21.173 --> 01:23:22.380
Like, that's the one
thing, I guess, as well,

01:23:22.380 --> 01:23:25.290
that I've just been like kind
of getting back used to again,

01:23:25.290 --> 01:23:27.900
because it's like, I personally
have been stuck in Japan

01:23:27.900 --> 01:23:29.010
for the past three years now,

01:23:29.010 --> 01:23:32.520
and it's like stranger friendliness
is not as big of a thing

01:23:32.520 --> 01:23:33.960
as it is, say, in like the UK, right?

01:23:33.960 --> 01:23:34.954
- [Garnt] Yeah, yeah.

01:23:34.954 --> 01:23:36.357
- Especially in a con
setting, so it's like,

01:23:36.357 --> 01:23:38.490
I'm just getting used
to just random people

01:23:38.490 --> 01:23:39.930
just being like, "Hey."

01:23:39.930 --> 01:23:42.035
- Yeah, we've gone from like-
- It's strange.

01:23:42.035 --> 01:23:44.821
- I feel like it has been
like just us readjusting

01:23:44.821 --> 01:23:46.804
and reacclimating to con culture

01:23:46.804 --> 01:23:48.294
'cause it's been like such a...

01:23:48.294 --> 01:23:50.992
We've gone from like zero to like 200%

01:23:50.992 --> 01:23:52.711
(Joey laughing)

01:23:52.711 --> 01:23:53.850
in like the span of a day.

01:23:53.850 --> 01:23:55.740
And it just like, I'd forgotten, one,

01:23:55.740 --> 01:23:57.810
how intense it was before,

01:23:57.810 --> 01:23:59.790
like before COVID and everything.

01:23:59.790 --> 01:24:02.460
And now, it's like even
more intense 'cause, one,

01:24:02.460 --> 01:24:03.293
COVID'S happened,

01:24:03.293 --> 01:24:07.620
everyone's even more
excited and enthusiastic.

01:24:07.620 --> 01:24:10.080
And also, we are way more recognizable.

01:24:10.080 --> 01:24:12.090
So it's just kind of like all culminated

01:24:12.090 --> 01:24:14.258
into this massive stirring pot.

01:24:14.258 --> 01:24:16.440
- I know like for me it was...

01:24:16.440 --> 01:24:17.407
I caught myself being like,

01:24:17.407 --> 01:24:18.570
"Oh man, it's been such a long time

01:24:18.570 --> 01:24:19.590
since I've been to a con,"

01:24:19.590 --> 01:24:21.420
because there's so many
times during the signing,

01:24:21.420 --> 01:24:23.940
where like, 'cause you're
meeting so many people,

01:24:23.940 --> 01:24:26.850
you start to get into like
a pattern of things to say.

01:24:26.850 --> 01:24:28.860
It's like, you start off with the hello.

01:24:28.860 --> 01:24:30.270
Like, "How's your con experience been?

01:24:30.270 --> 01:24:31.710
How's your day been?" whatever.

01:24:31.710 --> 01:24:33.600
And then (chuckles)
there was so many times

01:24:33.600 --> 01:24:35.000
where like people would be like,

01:24:35.000 --> 01:24:37.110
"I hope you enjoy your time in the UK."

01:24:37.110 --> 01:24:38.508
And I'd be like, "Yeah, you too."

01:24:38.508 --> 01:24:39.840
(Garnt laughing)

01:24:39.840 --> 01:24:41.940
As if they're not from here. (chuckles)

01:24:41.940 --> 01:24:43.020
- Well, there was a lot of people actually

01:24:43.020 --> 01:24:44.100
who are like not from the UK.

01:24:44.100 --> 01:24:46.290
- Yeah, but it's like clearly,

01:24:46.290 --> 01:24:48.450
every time I said "you
too" to that question,

01:24:48.450 --> 01:24:51.120
it was always the most like
British sounding person ever.

01:24:51.120 --> 01:24:53.730
I was like, yeah, as if
they don't live here.

01:24:53.730 --> 01:24:55.200
It's like, "Ah, damn it."

01:24:55.200 --> 01:24:56.547
- I think I said that a
few times, not to that,

01:24:56.547 --> 01:24:58.320
but like, "Oh, thanks a
lot for your content,"

01:24:58.320 --> 01:24:59.153
I go, "You too."

01:24:59.153 --> 01:25:02.220
(Joey and Garnt laughing)

01:25:02.220 --> 01:25:03.617
- It's like, "How did you know?"

01:25:05.192 --> 01:25:07.020
- Okay, it's not a con experience.

01:25:07.020 --> 01:25:10.740
We had a cab back, me and
Joey and a few other friends.

01:25:10.740 --> 01:25:15.395
And it was like 41 pounds, this cab ride.

01:25:15.395 --> 01:25:16.950
This, this cab ride.

01:25:16.950 --> 01:25:17.783
- Yeah, yeah.

01:25:17.783 --> 01:25:18.960
- And you know, I went to go pay.

01:25:18.960 --> 01:25:20.880
I gave the guy, 'cause
I only had like 10s,

01:25:20.880 --> 01:25:22.683
so I gave the guy 50, right?

01:25:23.640 --> 01:25:25.027
So, in my head, I'm like,

01:25:25.027 --> 01:25:26.730
"Okay, it's been like three years

01:25:26.730 --> 01:25:29.247
or like since I've been
like tipping normally."

01:25:29.247 --> 01:25:31.290
and I know that sometimes
you tip cab drivers

01:25:31.290 --> 01:25:32.514
in London and stuff, and I was like,

01:25:32.514 --> 01:25:33.810
"Okay, yeah, yeah, I forgot about this."

01:25:33.810 --> 01:25:35.790
'Cause I never took cabs
when I lived here before.

01:25:35.790 --> 01:25:36.627
Obviously, it was late,

01:25:36.627 --> 01:25:38.310
and we were in like the middle of nowhere.

01:25:38.310 --> 01:25:41.407
So, I pay this guy, and then he's like,

01:25:41.407 --> 01:25:43.860
"Oh yeah, yeah, yeah,
I'll give you the change.

01:25:43.860 --> 01:25:45.480
Just get out the car, and
I'll give you the change."

01:25:45.480 --> 01:25:47.640
So I get out the car, and
I'm kind of just tired,

01:25:47.640 --> 01:25:48.473
it's like 3:00 AM.

01:25:48.473 --> 01:25:50.250
Like, "Bro, I just wanna go to bed."

01:25:50.250 --> 01:25:52.627
And so the guy, I was like,

01:25:52.627 --> 01:25:54.300
"All right, so can I have my change?"

01:25:54.300 --> 01:25:56.640
'Cause the way I tip, I
don't know if you do this,

01:25:56.640 --> 01:25:58.680
I want all my change first-

01:25:58.680 --> 01:25:59.610
- And then you give some back?

01:25:59.610 --> 01:26:01.980
- Then I will be like, "Here's
here's your tip," right?

01:26:01.980 --> 01:26:02.813
- Yeah
- Yeah.

01:26:02.813 --> 01:26:06.390
- And so (chuckles) I was like,
"Oh, can I have my change?"

01:26:06.390 --> 01:26:08.841
And he was like, "What?"

01:26:08.841 --> 01:26:09.871
(Garnt laughing)

01:26:09.871 --> 01:26:11.523
And he looked at me like.

01:26:13.200 --> 01:26:15.840
I asked for change, and
then he just looked at me

01:26:15.840 --> 01:26:18.420
like he wanted me to take it back.

01:26:18.420 --> 01:26:19.614
Like he wanted me to pretend like I did-

01:26:19.614 --> 01:26:20.447
- Say sorry.

01:26:20.447 --> 01:26:21.280
- Say sorry.
- Yeah.

01:26:21.280 --> 01:26:24.690
I was like, "Bro, what the fuck?"

01:26:24.690 --> 01:26:28.501
I was gonna tip him, and now
he's being weird about it,

01:26:28.501 --> 01:26:29.760
and now I wana tip him less.

01:26:29.760 --> 01:26:32.640
'Cause I'm like, "Just
gimme my fuckin'..."

01:26:32.640 --> 01:26:35.010
I'm like, "Nine pounds is a lot," right?

01:26:35.010 --> 01:26:38.085
This is not America. We don't tip 20%.

01:26:38.085 --> 01:26:41.400
I was gonna give him like
a five. That was my plan.

01:26:41.400 --> 01:26:43.500
And then I was like, "You're
being weird about this, man.

01:26:43.500 --> 01:26:44.924
Just gimme my fuckin' money back,

01:26:44.924 --> 01:26:45.790
and I'll give you some back."

01:26:45.790 --> 01:26:48.057
I was like, "What the fuck, dude?"

01:26:48.990 --> 01:26:49.823
- That's not cool.

01:26:49.823 --> 01:26:50.950
- And so, I'm like,
"All right, yeah, yeah."

01:26:50.950 --> 01:26:52.290
I was like, "Can I have my change?"

01:26:52.290 --> 01:26:53.520
And then he like looks at me.

01:26:53.520 --> 01:26:55.800
Again, I wanna say it was the most awkward

01:26:55.800 --> 01:26:57.660
five to 10 seconds of my life.

01:26:57.660 --> 01:26:59.910
I felt like Za Warudo in Jojo.

01:26:59.910 --> 01:27:02.550
I could feel the one second, two seconds.

01:27:02.550 --> 01:27:06.287
And I feel like he was trying
to figure out if I was drunk,

01:27:06.287 --> 01:27:09.093
I was fine, but I felt like
he was trying to see if like,

01:27:09.093 --> 01:27:11.207
he was like, (inhales deeply)
"Can I get away with this?"

01:27:11.207 --> 01:27:12.900
(all chuckling)

01:27:12.900 --> 01:27:15.270
And so he goes into his car,
he like rummages around,

01:27:15.270 --> 01:27:18.240
and he comes out, and he
just gives me five pounds.

01:27:18.240 --> 01:27:23.240
And I'm like, "Dude,
all right, okay, fine."

01:27:24.660 --> 01:27:25.493
- He's probably thinking like,

01:27:25.493 --> 01:27:27.030
"Maybe if I just give him some money,

01:27:27.030 --> 01:27:27.863
he might just shut up about it.

01:27:27.863 --> 01:27:30.240
- I was gonna give you
the five pound notes.

01:27:30.240 --> 01:27:32.460
Now you got four pound
because you're being a dick.

01:27:32.460 --> 01:27:33.293
- Yeah.

01:27:33.293 --> 01:27:35.670
- And I'm like, "Just gimme my money back,

01:27:35.670 --> 01:27:36.540
and I'll tip you!"

01:27:36.540 --> 01:27:38.490
It's like, "What the fuck?!"

01:27:38.490 --> 01:27:40.740
And I was just like,
"What a weird experience."

01:27:40.740 --> 01:27:42.480
Meanwhile, the people in the
car were just like vibing.

01:27:42.480 --> 01:27:44.670
They know that I'm like
having like this mind battle

01:27:44.670 --> 01:27:45.503
with this cab driver.

01:27:45.503 --> 01:27:46.336
It's like, "Just tip him."

01:27:46.336 --> 01:27:48.810
I was gonna give him money,
and he was making it weird.

01:27:48.810 --> 01:27:51.443
I was like, "Why are people like this?"

01:27:51.443 --> 01:27:54.120
- Everyone else was in the car
just like kind of chatting,

01:27:54.120 --> 01:27:57.810
and I'm just like dead
on the fuckin' backseat,

01:27:57.810 --> 01:27:59.220
not knowing that this is happening.

01:27:59.220 --> 01:28:00.507
- I was just like, "Bro, okay."

01:28:00.507 --> 01:28:02.250
And so he got his four pound tip.

01:28:02.250 --> 01:28:03.420
Jokes on you, you'd have
got a five pound tip

01:28:03.420 --> 01:28:05.823
if you'd just giving
me all my change, dude.

01:28:08.010 --> 01:28:09.869
This is just a weird experience
you don't get in Japan.

01:28:09.869 --> 01:28:12.390
(Connor laughing)

01:28:12.390 --> 01:28:14.190
They just give you it back immediately,

01:28:14.190 --> 01:28:15.630
and you never have to deal with this.

01:28:15.630 --> 01:28:18.330
And it was just so weird
just seeing the guy

01:28:18.330 --> 01:28:20.820
just not wanna give me my fuckin' change,

01:28:20.820 --> 01:28:21.653
and I was just like-

01:28:21.653 --> 01:28:23.076
- It's like, "Me no speak English."

01:28:23.076 --> 01:28:25.170
(Garnt and Joey chuckling)

01:28:25.170 --> 01:28:26.232
- That was weird.

01:28:26.232 --> 01:28:27.065
- It's just like, yeah,

01:28:27.065 --> 01:28:28.200
talking about like transport
in London, I guess.

01:28:28.200 --> 01:28:29.880
Like, I guess like there has been

01:28:29.880 --> 01:28:33.240
like a talk of the town since we got here.

01:28:33.240 --> 01:28:35.730
Because everyone that I've hung out with

01:28:35.730 --> 01:28:38.640
can't stop talking about
this Elizabeth line

01:28:38.640 --> 01:28:39.880
that has just fuckin' opened up.

01:28:39.880 --> 01:28:40.857
- Yeah, I like heard about it,

01:28:40.857 --> 01:28:43.290
and it's like some like fancy new line

01:28:43.290 --> 01:28:44.620
that's like recently
opened up or something.

01:28:44.620 --> 01:28:49.200
- Yeah, so apparently, it's
this line that's been planned

01:28:49.200 --> 01:28:51.240
that was meant to open,
I believe, in like-

01:28:51.240 --> 01:28:52.073
- Oh many years ago.

01:28:52.073 --> 01:28:55.110
- Yeah, yeah, like 2020, I
believe, that it's opened?

01:28:55.110 --> 01:28:57.300
- Nothing in the UK
ever gets done on time.

01:28:57.300 --> 01:28:58.950
- Yeah. (chuckles)

01:28:58.950 --> 01:29:00.663
And then it got delayed.
- Nothing.

01:29:00.663 --> 01:29:03.990
- It got delayed, but
like the hype was real.

01:29:03.990 --> 01:29:05.610
I thought like, "I'm coming to London,

01:29:05.610 --> 01:29:07.053
I'm coming to a convention,
people would be like,

01:29:07.053 --> 01:29:09.750
'Oh, have you started
watching "Spike's Family?"

01:29:09.750 --> 01:29:10.620
Are you watching any new anime?'"

01:29:10.620 --> 01:29:11.557
No, everyone's like,

01:29:11.557 --> 01:29:12.772
"Yo, you've been on the Elizabeth line."

01:29:12.772 --> 01:29:13.830
(Joey laughing)
"Have you been

01:29:13.830 --> 01:29:15.237
on the Elizabeth line?"

01:29:16.329 --> 01:29:17.817
Like I haven't yet.
- I haven't yet.

01:29:17.817 --> 01:29:18.650
- I haven't.

01:29:18.650 --> 01:29:19.830
And I swear to God,

01:29:19.830 --> 01:29:22.410
someone could just like have
given birth the day before,

01:29:22.410 --> 01:29:24.330
and I'd be like, "Baby, nah, bruh.

01:29:24.330 --> 01:29:26.784
Elizabeth line, that's the real hype, man.

01:29:26.784 --> 01:29:28.170
I gotta try

01:29:28.170 --> 01:29:29.003
the Elizabeth line."
- Real shit.

01:29:29.003 --> 01:29:29.836
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

01:29:29.836 --> 01:29:31.297
But from what I heard, it's just like,

01:29:31.297 --> 01:29:34.154
"It's a air conditioned
line," and I'm just like,

01:29:34.154 --> 01:29:35.774
"Isn't that just every train in Japan?"

01:29:35.774 --> 01:29:37.020
(all laughing)

01:29:37.020 --> 01:29:38.640
- And heated seats.

01:29:38.640 --> 01:29:39.780
- I didn't notice that actually,

01:29:39.780 --> 01:29:42.030
it's like the series of questions we got

01:29:42.030 --> 01:29:45.240
were very different to
how the list of questions

01:29:45.240 --> 01:29:46.337
I would normally get at signing.

01:29:46.337 --> 01:29:48.934
'Cause like before Trash
Taste, it was always like,

01:29:48.934 --> 01:29:49.980
"What do you think about this anime?

01:29:49.980 --> 01:29:50.970
What do you think about this manga? "

01:29:50.970 --> 01:29:54.360
And there was like definitely
some amounts of those.

01:29:54.360 --> 01:29:57.960
But I think the top three
questions I received

01:29:57.960 --> 01:30:00.757
during that entire
weekend, number one was,

01:30:00.757 --> 01:30:02.558
"Have you had a Tesco meal deal yet?"

01:30:02.558 --> 01:30:03.391
(Garnt laughs)

01:30:03.391 --> 01:30:05.553
Number two was, "Have
you been to Greggs yet?"

01:30:05.553 --> 01:30:07.027
- Yes!
- And number three was,

01:30:07.027 --> 01:30:08.567
"Have you been to Spoons yet?"

01:30:08.567 --> 01:30:09.810
(all laughing)

01:30:09.810 --> 01:30:11.640
Like nothing to do with anime.

01:30:11.640 --> 01:30:14.070
It was all just like, "Have
you had these things?"

01:30:14.070 --> 01:30:15.090
- Have you had any of them?

01:30:15.090 --> 01:30:17.130
- Well, yeah, you took me to
a Spoons last time I was here,

01:30:17.130 --> 01:30:18.946
but apparently, you took me
into like the worst Spoons.

01:30:18.946 --> 01:30:20.730
- Yeah, it was the worst
Spoons. It was the worst Spoon.

01:30:20.730 --> 01:30:22.003
- But no, I still haven't had

01:30:22.003 --> 01:30:22.903
a Tesco meal deal yet.
- Oh, bro,

01:30:22.903 --> 01:30:23.760
I really want a Greggs.

01:30:23.760 --> 01:30:25.380
- I haven't had a Greggs yet at all.

01:30:25.380 --> 01:30:27.298
So I mean, we're here for a little, so.

01:30:27.298 --> 01:30:29.790
- I've forgotten how passionate
people are about Greggs.

01:30:29.790 --> 01:30:30.881
- [Joey] Yeah.

01:30:30.881 --> 01:30:31.714
- It's very good.

01:30:31.714 --> 01:30:32.547
- Greggs is the bakery?

01:30:32.547 --> 01:30:33.690
- Yeah, it's the bakery.
- Okay, yeah, yeah.

01:30:33.690 --> 01:30:34.938
- It's so more than that, though.

01:30:34.938 --> 01:30:35.771
- Yeah, it is.

01:30:35.771 --> 01:30:36.604
(Joey laughing)

01:30:36.604 --> 01:30:37.913
It's the experience.
- It's so much more than that.

01:30:37.913 --> 01:30:39.604
Just a bakery, dude.

01:30:39.604 --> 01:30:41.550
- Like I feel like you have
to go there at least once

01:30:41.550 --> 01:30:44.163
to get your British passport,
that's the last test.

01:30:45.480 --> 01:30:46.890
- Because it's really weird

01:30:46.890 --> 01:30:50.370
'cause I didn't realize
how unknown Greggs was

01:30:50.370 --> 01:30:52.950
to people outside of England.

01:30:52.950 --> 01:30:54.810
Because a lot of people British people,

01:30:54.810 --> 01:30:57.480
we speak about Nando's,
we speak about Spoons,

01:30:57.480 --> 01:31:00.360
but like not a lot of people
speak about Greggs abroad,

01:31:00.360 --> 01:31:02.340
and it's just one of these British things

01:31:02.340 --> 01:31:03.776
that if you're in England,

01:31:03.776 --> 01:31:07.110
you would've been to a Greggs
at least once in your life.

01:31:07.110 --> 01:31:09.030
You might not always talk about it,

01:31:09.030 --> 01:31:12.000
but it's part of being British.

01:31:12.000 --> 01:31:15.240
And I didn't realize this
until I came back to England,

01:31:15.240 --> 01:31:17.400
and everyone started asking me

01:31:17.400 --> 01:31:20.430
if I'd gone back to Greggs yet. (chuckles)

01:31:20.430 --> 01:31:22.470
- It's important. Greggs
is an important thing.

01:31:22.470 --> 01:31:24.960
I feel from what I heard from people,

01:31:24.960 --> 01:31:29.100
like I feel being British
person and not going to Greggs

01:31:29.100 --> 01:31:32.850
is like being a Japanese person
and not going to FamilyMart.

01:31:32.850 --> 01:31:35.410
It's like that level of
like, how have you not-

01:31:35.410 --> 01:31:37.517
- To me, it's even more than FamilyMart.

01:31:37.517 --> 01:31:40.323
'cause you can find
FamilyMart all over Asia.

01:31:41.190 --> 01:31:42.270
It's like all over Asia.

01:31:42.270 --> 01:31:43.500
- I didn't know that.

01:31:43.500 --> 01:31:44.333
- Yeah, yeah,

01:31:44.333 --> 01:31:45.679
there's like FamilyMarts
in Thailand, actually.

01:31:45.679 --> 01:31:46.679
- Oh, I didn't know that.

01:31:46.679 --> 01:31:47.512
- It's like 7 Elevens.
- I didn't know that either.

01:31:47.512 --> 01:31:48.477
- This is news to me.

01:31:48.477 --> 01:31:49.310
- Yeah, yeah, yeah, exactly.

01:31:49.310 --> 01:31:51.180
So it's not like a specific...

01:31:51.180 --> 01:31:52.620
It's obviously very Japanese,

01:31:52.620 --> 01:31:55.050
so like I'm gonna assume
it started in Japan,

01:31:55.050 --> 01:31:56.100
but it's like expanded,

01:31:56.100 --> 01:32:00.570
but like I believe Greggs
is only available in the UK.

01:32:00.570 --> 01:32:03.270
And it's nothing-

01:32:03.270 --> 01:32:05.070
- So there's like a really British pride.

01:32:05.070 --> 01:32:06.840
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.
- So, it's cheap,

01:32:06.840 --> 01:32:08.223
and it tastes amazing.

01:32:09.060 --> 01:32:09.893
Yeah, what's not to like?

01:32:09.893 --> 01:32:11.460
- Best sausage rolls, man.

01:32:11.460 --> 01:32:13.483
- Why haven't you guys taken
me there yet? I wanna go.

01:32:13.483 --> 01:32:14.890
- I actually haven't seen any.

01:32:14.890 --> 01:32:16.837
- It's like the hype
is so real in my head.

01:32:16.837 --> 01:32:19.200
I'm like, not only have
you guys like hyped it up,

01:32:19.200 --> 01:32:22.200
but like every second British
person I met this weekend

01:32:22.200 --> 01:32:23.189
is like, "Greggs, though,

01:32:23.189 --> 01:32:24.022
bro, Greggs."
- Let me see

01:32:24.022 --> 01:32:25.750
where the nearest Greggs is.

01:32:25.750 --> 01:32:26.583
- Yeah, real shit.

01:32:26.583 --> 01:32:27.720
- Let me have a look at that real shit.

01:32:27.720 --> 01:32:29.550
Yeah, get your boys some Greggs.

01:32:29.550 --> 01:32:31.087
And then there were people being like,

01:32:31.087 --> 01:32:33.240
"Yo, so like have you been a Tescos yet?"

01:32:33.240 --> 01:32:34.425
Have you had the Tesco meal deal?"

01:32:34.425 --> 01:32:35.258
And I was like, "Not yet."

01:32:35.258 --> 01:32:37.560
And I knew it was like real shit

01:32:37.560 --> 01:32:38.393
because like people will like,

01:32:38.393 --> 01:32:40.680
"All right, here's my recommendation.

01:32:40.680 --> 01:32:42.090
These are the ones to avoid.

01:32:42.090 --> 01:32:43.590
These are the ones that
you should go for."

01:32:43.590 --> 01:32:45.120
And I didn't realize there were

01:32:45.120 --> 01:32:46.830
so many different meal deals.

01:32:46.830 --> 01:32:49.154
And like there were people
like in the signing, right?

01:32:49.154 --> 01:32:50.437
There would be like a person
in front of me being like,

01:32:50.437 --> 01:32:52.440
"All right, so here's the
meal deal I recommend."

01:32:52.440 --> 01:32:53.520
And I knew it was a real shit

01:32:53.520 --> 01:32:55.770
when like the person behind
them would like interject

01:32:55.770 --> 01:32:56.754
and be like, "No, no, no, no.

01:32:56.754 --> 01:32:58.072
(all laugh)

01:32:58.072 --> 01:33:01.553
Don't spread misinformation like that.

01:33:01.553 --> 01:33:02.386
This is the real shit."

01:33:02.386 --> 01:33:05.610
And I was just like, "Guys, chill out."

01:33:05.610 --> 01:33:07.020
- There's a Greg's 10
minutes away from him.

01:33:07.020 --> 01:33:07.985
- Fuck ya, let's go.

01:33:07.985 --> 01:33:08.818
(Connor laughing)

01:33:08.818 --> 01:33:09.651
- Let's walk off to London.
- After this episode.

01:33:09.651 --> 01:33:11.037
- After, after.
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

01:33:11.037 --> 01:33:14.370
But yeah, I mean like we
talk about Tesco meal deals,

01:33:14.370 --> 01:33:16.980
but a meal deal is like a lot of choice.

01:33:16.980 --> 01:33:20.100
So you need to like
have the optimal order.

01:33:20.100 --> 01:33:21.870
- Yeah, I mean, there's just like...

01:33:21.870 --> 01:33:24.930
It's like Blackjack, there's
the perfect way to play it.

01:33:24.930 --> 01:33:26.730
That's what a meal deal is, right?

01:33:26.730 --> 01:33:29.520
So you need to need to learn
how to count cards, okay?

01:33:29.520 --> 01:33:30.960
Pick the right meal deal.

01:33:30.960 --> 01:33:33.180
'Cause you know, there's
certain items in the meal deal

01:33:33.180 --> 01:33:35.400
that you can get where if you
were to buy them individually,

01:33:35.400 --> 01:33:37.160
it would cost like two pound 50.

01:33:37.160 --> 01:33:39.930
So you can kind of min
max the price options.

01:33:39.930 --> 01:33:41.250
So don't be buying water.

01:33:41.250 --> 01:33:44.760
Don't get like a fuckin'
little fruit thing,

01:33:44.760 --> 01:33:47.520
maximize your cost performance.

01:33:47.520 --> 01:33:50.100
- Yeah, you don't wanna
go for Walker's crisps.

01:33:50.100 --> 01:33:52.230
- McCoy's crisp, the big boys as well.

01:33:52.230 --> 01:33:53.063
- Or the (indistinct)

01:33:53.063 --> 01:33:54.105
- Or Walker's MAX.
- Walker's MAX.

01:33:54.105 --> 01:33:55.470
- You can't just go

01:33:55.470 --> 01:33:57.810
to like the little fuckin'
basic gas vanilla water.

01:33:57.810 --> 01:33:59.430
- You can get like an
Innocent Smoothie as well.

01:33:59.430 --> 01:34:00.295
There only like two pounds thirty.

01:34:00.295 --> 01:34:03.217
- You literally sound like
every person at the signing.

01:34:03.217 --> 01:34:04.410
- It's important. It's important.

01:34:04.410 --> 01:34:05.730
- I knew it was real as well

01:34:05.730 --> 01:34:07.920
because there was like
a bunch of people also,

01:34:07.920 --> 01:34:09.810
like when they mentioned
the Tesco meal deal,

01:34:09.810 --> 01:34:11.557
they came up to me and they were like,

01:34:11.557 --> 01:34:13.320
"Yeah, Tesco meal deals are amazing,

01:34:13.320 --> 01:34:16.950
but they opted it by 50 P, and
it's an absolute travesty."

01:34:16.950 --> 01:34:17.783
And I'm just like,

01:34:17.783 --> 01:34:19.247
"I wish I could feel your anger right now

01:34:19.247 --> 01:34:21.240
'cause it seems very real."

01:34:21.240 --> 01:34:23.130
- There's one like a one-minute
walk, not even one minute,

01:34:23.130 --> 01:34:24.870
like it's literally opposite our hotel.

01:34:24.870 --> 01:34:26.820
- Oh, fuck yeah!

01:34:26.820 --> 01:34:28.680
- There was this article in the UK

01:34:28.680 --> 01:34:31.170
that some doctor was calling
for meal deals to be banned

01:34:31.170 --> 01:34:32.520
because they're too unhealthy.

01:34:32.520 --> 01:34:33.353
- Really?

01:34:33.353 --> 01:34:35.730
- And they're too like appealing.

01:34:35.730 --> 01:34:37.260
- Yeah. (laughs) Appealing.

01:34:37.260 --> 01:34:40.260
- Because people just buy
these like every day for lunch

01:34:40.260 --> 01:34:41.880
'cause it's such good value for money,

01:34:41.880 --> 01:34:43.680
and they taste fuckin' amazing,

01:34:43.680 --> 01:34:45.390
but they're really bad for you.

01:34:45.390 --> 01:34:48.540
'Cause the sandwiches are
like absolutely just stuffed

01:34:48.540 --> 01:34:49.653
with awful stuff.

01:34:50.526 --> 01:34:51.450
But it's like a McDonald's burger,

01:34:51.450 --> 01:34:53.040
it's like, you don't wanna
know what goes in, but you know

01:34:53.040 --> 01:34:54.480
it tastes so amazing.
- But it tastes good, yeah.

01:34:54.480 --> 01:34:55.710
- Why does it taste so damn good?

01:34:55.710 --> 01:34:56.668
What does Ronald put in those-
- FamilyMart sandwiches

01:34:56.668 --> 01:34:58.669
are exactly the same as well, right?

01:34:58.669 --> 01:35:01.919
- Oh, yeah, you know the
sandwiches are not fresh at all,

01:35:01.919 --> 01:35:02.752
but like, yeah.

01:35:02.752 --> 01:35:03.630
- But they still taste good.

01:35:03.630 --> 01:35:04.590
- They taste really fuckin' good.

01:35:04.590 --> 01:35:07.023
- Yeah, I guess, it's like going back to

01:35:07.023 --> 01:35:09.540
like why people are
recommending you what to order.

01:35:09.540 --> 01:35:11.730
It's kinda like going to a
Chinese restaurant from here

01:35:11.730 --> 01:35:13.680
and ordering like compow
chicken or something.

01:35:13.680 --> 01:35:15.024
And it's like, "I've had Chinese food."

01:35:15.024 --> 01:35:15.857
(Joey laughing)

01:35:15.857 --> 01:35:16.690
And then everyone would be like,

01:35:16.690 --> 01:35:18.450
"No, you have not had Chinese food."

01:35:18.450 --> 01:35:19.283
You know what I mean?

01:35:19.283 --> 01:35:20.374
- It's like going on Pan Express.

